cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "sortlab: geometric sorting vs per-unit comparison, measured"
message: "If you reference these results, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "TETRA CA PBC"
    website: "https://tetra-ca.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tetra-ca/geometric-sort-lab"
url: "https://tetra-ca.com"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained C++17 benchmark comparing radix (geometric) sorting against
  comparator-based sorting across eight controlled sweeps: scale, key entropy,
  lane count and row layout, presortedness, payload width, small-n behavior,
  top-k selection, and SIMD contribution. Every sweep varies exactly one
  parameter, and every result is reproducible with a single `make` on the
  reader's own machine.
keywords:
  - sorting
  - radix sort
  - benchmark
  - simd
  - high-performance computing
  - cpp
license: Apache-2.0
